PREAMBLE  [ADAPT]
============================================================================

This Work (defined in Section 1) is created and stewarded by
<|author_name_indigenous|> <|author_name|> (the "Licensor"), a member of the
<|tribal_nation_name|> (the "Nation"), a federally recognized sovereign
tribal nation. [OPTIONAL — descendant-community sentence:] The Licensor is
also a descendant of <|community_description|>, whose rights and protocols
this License likewise protects, whether their families are enrolled in the
Nation or in any other federally recognized tribe.

This License is grounded in the inherent sovereignty of Indigenous peoples —
predating the United States Constitution and never surrendered — to protect,
control, and govern their intellectual and cultural property. It expressly
integrates:

    (a)  United States copyright law, including the doctrine that license
         CONDITIONS are enforceable as limits on the scope of permission
         (Jacobsen v. Katzer, 535 F.3d 1373 (Fed. Cir. 2008));
    (b)  Federal Indian law, including the reserved rights doctrine, the
         Indian canons of construction, treaty rights under
         <|specific_treaty_1_name_year_stat_cite|> and
         <|specific_treaty_2_name_year_stat_cite|>, and the consent doctrine
         of Montana v. United States, 450 U.S. 544, 565 (1981);
    (c)  Traditional Knowledge (TK) Labels (Local Contexts initiative);
    (d)  CARE Principles for Indigenous Data Governance (Carroll et al.,
         Data Science Journal 19:43 (2020), DOI 10.5334/dsj-2020-043) and
         IEEE 2890-2025 (Provenance of Indigenous Peoples' Data);
    (e)  International Indigenous-rights instruments, each according to its
         TRUE legal status as stated in Annex A (see the TRUTH RULE in the
         header comment);
    (f)  The laws, customs, and traditions of the Nation and of
         <|community_description|>.

Nothing herein claims for an individual Licensor the sovereign immunity that
belongs only to tribal governments (Section 16). Nothing herein takes sides
in any inter-tribal dispute; it protects the Work and the Community's
cultural patrimony across enrollment lines.

============================================================================
1. DEFINITIONS AND TRADITIONAL KNOWLEDGE TAXONOMY
============================================================================

1.1  "Work" — the software, code, documentation, data structures, datasets,
     interfaces, designs, text, audio, video, language resources, and other
     original expression distributed under this License, with all associated
     Traditional Knowledge and Cultural Expressions, whether or not
     separately copyrightable.

1.2  "Traditional Knowledge" (TK) — knowledge, know-how, practices,
     innovations, and learning systems developed, sustained, and transmitted
     within the Community, including ecological, fisheries, navigational,
     linguistic, medicinal, and spiritual knowledge embodied in or informing
     the Work (following WIPO IGC usage).

1.3  "Traditional Cultural Expression" (TCE) — forms in which TK and culture
     are expressed, including music, dance, design, oral literature,
     ceremony, nomenclature, and visual art.

1.4  "Associated Traditional Knowledge" — as in the WIPO Treaty on
     Intellectual Property, Genetic Resources and Associated Traditional
     Knowledge (adopted May 24, 2024): TK associated with genetic resources
     used or claimed in an invention.

1.5  "Cultural Patrimony" — as in NAGPRA, 25 U.S.C. § 3001(3): objects of
     ongoing historical, traditional, or cultural importance central to the
     Community, inalienable by any individual.

1.6  "Derivative Data" — any data, dataset, corpus, embedding, feature
     representation, statistical model, annotation set, or index derived in
     whole or part from the Work or its outputs.

1.7  "Model" — any machine-learning model, neural network, classifier, or
     similar system, including weights and parameters, trained or fine-tuned
     in whole or part on the Work or Derivative Data.

1.8  "Community" — (i) <|tribal_nation_name|> and its members; and any
     additional ancestor-descendant communities identified here:
     <|community_description|>, whether or not their members hold enrollment
     in the Nation or any other federally recognized tribe.

1.9  "Community Protocols" — the laws, customs, and traditions governing the
     Community's TK, TCEs, and Cultural Patrimony, as recorded or
     incorporated in Annex B.

1.10 "Consensual Relationship" — the relationship formed between the
     Licensor and each Licensee by acceptance of this License, being a
     consensual relationship "through commercial dealing, contracts, leases,
     or other arrangements" within the meaning of Montana v. United States,
     450 U.S. at 565.

1.11 "Treaty-Protected Interests" — <|treaty_reserved_rights_summary|>,
     reserved in <|specific_treaty_1_name_year_stat_cite|> and
     <|specific_treaty_2_name_year_stat_cite|>, together with aboriginal and
     inherent rights never ceded.

1.12 "Licensee" — any person or entity, public or private, that uses,
     reproduces, modifies, distributes, or prepares derivative works of the
     Work, in any medium, in whole or part.

