2. GRANT OF RIGHTS AND LICENSE CONDITIONS
============================================================================

2.1  LIMITED GRANT. Subject to full and continuing compliance with every
     condition herein, the Licensor grants a non-exclusive, non-transferable,
     non-sublicensable, revocable license to use, reproduce, and modify the
     Work solely for Permissible Uses (Section 11). No other rights are
     granted.

2.2  CONDITIONS, NOT MERE COVENANTS. Every requirement of this License is a
     CONDITION limiting the scope of the grant. Non-compliance places the
     Licensee outside the license's scope and constitutes copyright
     infringement, exposing the Licensee to all Copyright Act remedies,
     including injunctions (17 U.S.C. § 502), actual damages and profits
     (§ 504(b)), statutory damages (§ 504(c)), and fees (§ 505). Jacobsen v.
     Katzer, 535 F.3d 1373 (Fed. Cir. 2008).

2.3  ACCEPTANCE. Use, reproduction, modification, distribution, or
     derivative preparation of the Work, or click-through assent, constitutes
     acceptance and forms the Consensual Relationship.

2.4  NO IMPLIED THIRD-PARTY LICENSES. This License travels with the Work;
     downstream recipients take rights only under this License from the
     Licensor.

2.5  DEFENSIVE SUSPENSION. Patent-assertion against the Work, the Licensor,
     or Community members with respect to their use of the Work terminates
     the asserting party's rights automatically.

