16. IDENTITY OF RIGHTS; NO WAIVER; IMMUNITY RESERVED
============================================================================

16.1 The Licensor asserts personal property rights, stewardship obligations
     for communal TK/TCE/Patrimony (inalienable, §8.1), and treaty-beneficiary
     cultural rights.

16.2 NO PERSONAL IMMUNITY CLAIM. Tribal sovereign immunity belongs to
     tribal governments and their arms/officials in official capacity
     (Bay Mills, 572 U.S. 782 (2014); Kiowa, 523 U.S. 751 (1998)); this
     License neither claims individual immunity for the Licensor nor waives
     or binds any tribal government's immunity.

16.3 ENFORCEMENT by the Licensor personally; any present or future tribal
     resolution recognizing this License supplements (never substitutes for)
     these private rights.

16.4 NO WAIVER by non-enforcement or acceptance of performance.

